  Interpolation error budget for lidar_tilt_joint:
    sweep        deg/sample    worst gap       at 3 m
    6 s (15 deg/s)       0.40         5.80       15.2 cm
    4 s (22.5)         0.60         8.70       22.8 cm
    2 s (45)           1.20        17.40       45.9 cm
    (worst gap = deg travelled across the LONGEST observed publish gap; the
     3 m column is the mid-gap linear-interpolation error, i.e. the deskew
     floor unless the tilt publisher is made faster AND regular.)

